    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L26-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "26.2: That’s a lot of Houses",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Han and Lin each have a method to calculate \\(3^5 + 3^6 + \\ldots + 3^n\\). Han says this is \\(3^5 \\left(1+ 3+ 3^2 + \\ldots +3^{n-5}\\right)\\) and concludes that \\(3^5+\\ldots + 3^n = 3^5\\frac{3^{n-4} -1}{3-1}\\). Lin says that this is a…",
